From 1ef7ce45e9c27276fed6491cc50e77ebc9205136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:00:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Drop-rate boost: realism two extra rare rolls, 5x one, 10x
 none

The second half of backlog item 6. A boosted kill gets extra draws on
~ultrarare_getitem; the rest of the monster's table is untouched, so nothing
about a normal kill changes.

ONE HOOK, NOT 363 EDITS. The xp half put its multiplier in Player.addXp
because there are 288 stat_advance sites and no wrapper, so content-side
would have meant editing all of them and the next skill anybody wrote would
have missed it. Same argument here: 363 random() calls across 214 drop-table
scripts, most not even the main ladder. [proc,npc_death] is the single funnel
every death already passes through - ~barrows_potential and ~boss_kill_record
are both hooked there for exactly that reason. Third hook, same funnel.

IT IS GATED, and that is the design decision. ~ultrarare_getitem is the
SHARED rare table, so granting a draw on it from any monster would let a
goblin pay out a dragon med helm - a new drop source rather than a rate
boost, and worst of all in realism, the mode meant to be authentic.
droprate_shared_rare lists the 182 monsters whose own table already reaches
that proc, so a boosted kill can only ever produce a drop that monster could
already have produced. Its rare slot simply comes up more often.

The list is derived by tools/gendroprate.py from which scripts call the proc
and which [ai_queue3] triggers those files carry, expanding _black_demon to
its two category members, and the battery re-derives the same set every run.
A table written later that routes into the shared rare slot is covered
automatically; one that does not cannot quietly acquire the boost.

IT IS ALLOWED TO WHIFF. ~ultrarare_getitem gives nothing on about 10.3% of
draws - 15/128 of its ladder delegates to ~megararetable, which pays on
15/128 and falls through otherwise, returning (null, 0) that obj_add
discards. A bonus draw has exactly a natural draw's odds, which is what makes
this statable as "the rare slot is rolled twice". Re-rolling until it paid
would make a bonus draw strictly better than a natural one and would mean
editing the proc all 63 callers depend on.

^xprate_unset (0) counts as realism, for the same reason the engine reads it
as 1x: a character never asked is on the authentic rate, and handing every
existing account the slowest xp and none of the compensation is a poor trade.

rs2check 1709 scripts / 499 configs, 0 ERROR, 0 CHECK; gamemode_battery
ALL PASS; gamemode_mutate 77/77, each caught by its own check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J1qUhTcu63bJ3hCBBxy7nU
